    <statement><p>Suppose that <m>\displaystyle f(x,y)= \sin(4 x+ 5 y)</m> is a function of two variables.</p>
<p><alert> 1.</alert> Find the gradient of <m>f(x,y).</m></p>
<p>Answer: <m>\nabla f(x,y) =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> 2.</alert> Evaluate the gradient at the point <m>P(-10,8).</m></p>
<p>Answer: <m>\nabla f(-10,8) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert> 3.</alert> Find the rate of change of <m>f(x,y)</m> at <m>P</m> in the direction of the vector <m>\mathbf{u} = \frac{1}{2}\left(\sqrt{3}\mathbf{i}-\mathbf{j}\right) .</m></p>
<p>Answer: <m>D_{\mathbf{u}}\,f(-10,8) =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;4\cos\mathopen{}\left(4x+5y\right),5\cos\mathopen{}\left(4x+5y\right)\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left&lt;4,5\right&gt;</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0.9641</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
